// The Wind Gate (Gate_1; bible 4.5, 4.0): the fledgling-leap. The clan sings the young off the lip; nobody has come
// up the updraft in forty years, since the Unmaking took the sky. Wren does: Windmemory. The wind knowing her is a
// plant for where she is from (5.3). The leap comes on the third day of the walk.

title: Gate_Idrenne_Leap
---
<<if flag("windreach.camp.night") < 2>>
    Idrenne: The Gate is the third day's. Walk the first two with us and you'll know why. #still #line:0f3e0ba
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("windreach.leap.done")>>
    Idrenne: Forty years we sang them off this lip. Then you. I was standing right here. #still #face:bright #line:0fc27e2
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Idrenne: This is the Gate. The young stand on the lip, and we sing, and they jump. #line:0ca651a
Idrenne: The updraft used to catch them. For forty years now it hasn't. We sing anyway. #face:grave #line:016bb6f
Idrenne: Nobody makes you. Nobody has, since the first one fell. #face:grave #line:0057f8a
-> I'll jump. #line:09106a6
    Idrenne: Then we'll sing. #line:03aa6d4
    <<voice warden windreach>>
-> What do you sing? #line:0a38587
    Idrenne: Where each of us was standing when we learned to fly. Nobody remembers. So we sing the places. #face:grave #line:066c0aa
    <<voice surveyor windreach>>
-> ... #line:01563b7
    Idrenne: Yes. That's how the brave ones stand, too. #face:bright #line:0283f3f
    <<voice drift windreach>>
Gate: She jumps. The song follows her down. Then the air remembers her, and holds. #line:09c9e54
Idrenne: Ha! Look at her. Brek, look. The wind knows you, map-bird. #line:05732f0
Idrenne: It knows where you're from better than you do. #plant:5.3 #face:bright #line:069d8bf
<<grant Windmemory>>
<<flag windreach.leap.done 1>>
===
